// VSCode workspace settings for the parcel-tracker monorepo.
//
// The mobile project owns the only TypeScript install in the repo (the
// backend is Python). When VSCode is opened at the monorepo root, it looks
// for `node_modules/typescript/` at the workspace root, doesn't find one,
// and falls back to its bundled TypeScript — which doesn't auto-include
// parcel-track-mobile/node_modules/@types/jest. That's how you end up with
// phantom "Cannot find name 'describe'" errors on the mobile test files
// even though `npx tsc --noEmit` and CI are clean.
//
// Pointing tsdk at the mobile TS fixes the type acquisition AND makes
// `>TypeScript: Select TypeScript Version → Use Workspace Version` work.
// See parcel-track-mobile/AGENTS.md → Editor setup.
{
  "typescript.tsdk": "parcel-track-mobile/node_modules/typescript/lib",
  "typescript.enablePromptUseWorkspaceTsdk": true
}
